ling_logs 2; successor_snapshot with snapshot_index 12, successor_applied_index 64, successor_last_index 64 and successor_store 13..64, so the leader's retained log began above its snapshot index; then rejoin_observe with restores_before/early/late all 0, partner_applied_index 64 equal to successor_applied_index 64, partner_store 61..62 and successor_store 63..64. The peer was therefore repaired without any InstallSnapshot even though the boundary was compacted away, so the TrailingLogs=0 loop cannot be generalised by the compaction condition alone: another difference between the two setups must be load-bearing. The unexplained element is that the peer's final store (61..62) differs from the leader's (63..64) while both report applied 64, which is consistent with the peer snapshooting on its own after catching up (all nodes share the small SnapshotThreshold in this case); that is recorded as the next discriminator rather than assumed. The two asserted results are unchanged in scope: both ran TrailingLogs=0 with a snapshot taken at the log end, and this observation does not address them. Until the difference is identified the finding must be presented as 'with TrailingLogs=0 and a snapshot taken at the log end' without claiming that a non-zero trailing configuration reproduces it.\\\",\n   \\\"knowledge\\\":[{\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"0b99111e65eb4d9faae97028d6140ff5-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":3,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"compaction condition necessary but not sufficient; backlog run converged\\\"}],\n   \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"The peer reached the leader's applied index 64 with zero InstallSnapshot installs in a configuration whose retained log began above the snapshot index, so the compaction condition is refuted as a sufficient trigger for this setup.\\\",\n     \\\"The peer's own store (61..62) differs from the leader's (63..64) at the same applied index, suggesting the peer took its own snapshot during catch-up.\\\"],\n   \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"One local run of one case, non-retained, executed with a -run filter that skipped the other three cases in the same file.\\\",\n     \\\"All nodes share the small SnapshotThreshold in this case, so the peer could snapshot on its own; that confound is not isolated.\\\",\n     \\\"The run budget ended before the mechanism could be traced with a receipt; the four-case harness is left in the draft for a future execution.\\\"]}],\n \\\"experiment\\\":{\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@q-backlog-trigger\\\",\\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"src-compact17\\\",\\\"src-repl17\\\",\\\"src-installsnap17\\\"],\n   \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Four cases of the sealed-partition five-node history in one harness: (TrailingLogs=0, no post-snapshot entries), (10,20), (25,20) and a backlog case (TrailingLogs=2, SnapshotThreshold=5, 15 ms-per-apply FSM, 60 uncommitted commands on the peer, the leader snapping on its own while its log runs ahead of its FSM).\\\",\n     \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"The backlog case meets the compacted-boundary condition when the leader's snapshot index is below its retained store's first index.\\\",\\\"Counting Restore calls identifies InstallSnapshot installs without touching production logic.\\\",\\\"Precondition guards skip rather than fail.\\\"],\n     \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"No network transport; the peer's own snapshotting under the shared small SnapshotThreshold is not disabled.\\\"],\n     \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"peers\\\":5,\\\"cases\\\":[[0,0,5,False],[10,20,5,False],[25,20,5,False],[2,0,60,True]]}},\n   \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"For each case, MakeClusterCustom(Peers=5, Bootstrap=true, Conf{TrailingLogs, SnapshotThreshold 1<<20 or 5, SnapshotInterval 1h or 10ms, HeartbeatTimeout/ElectionTimeout/LeaderLeaseTimeout 1s}, MakeFSMFunc returning a Restore-counting MockFSM, wrapped in a 15 ms-per-apply slow FSM for the backlog case). Isolate {leader, partner} from the other three in both directions; replicate \"'`uncommitted` commands from the leader to the partner only; wait for a successor among the others; for non-backlog cases apply one command and take a user snapshot at the log end, for the backlog case fire 60 applies without waiting and wait for the leader'\"'s own snapshot index to become non-zero; apply \"'`post` further commands; heal with FullyConnect; sample each node'\"'s state, indexes and store bounds plus the partner's Restore count over about 1.5 s.\\\"}}\njson.dump(d,open('update-17.json','w'),indent=2)\nprint('written')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-12_09-55-08-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update-17.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"{\"valid\": false, \"run_id\": \"8085826003f64081939807df782a8a05\", \"elapsed_seconds\": 2922.15946132, \"diagnostics\": [{\"details\": {}, \"code\": \"submission\", \"category\": \"semantic\", \"task\": \"\", \"candidate_version\": 0, \"object_ids\": [], \"paths\": [], \"material_ids\": [], \"message\": \"Measured conclusions require a fixed experiment; source-only answers use explained or unresolved\", \"allowed\": []}], \"meaning\": \"Read-only validation of these bytes and saved state; no acceptance, execution or budget reservation\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
